.TH VIMTUTOR 1 2026-11-08 "w64devkit" "w64devkit Manual"
.SH NAME
vimtutor \- start the Vim tutor on a scratch copy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vimtutor
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vimtutor
starts
.BR vim (1)
on a new copy of the Vim tutor, a lesson file to read and edit, so the
original is never changed.
The copy is a new file with a
.B .tmp
name, made by Vim's
.B tempname()
in the Windows temporary directory, and it is not deleted afterwards.
.PP
Vim runs with
.BR "\-N \-u NONE" ,
so it is not Vi compatible and reads no initialization files.
.SH OPTIONS
None of its own.
Arguments are passed to Vim after the commands that make the copy.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR TMP ", " TEMP
The directory for the copy, chosen as Windows chooses a temporary
directory.
.TP
.B SHELL
Removed before Vim starts, as for
.BR vim ,
so that Vim's shell is
.BR cmd.exe .
.SH NOTES
Only the English tutor is installed, and there is no
.B \-g
option to use gvim.
This page replaces the upstream
.B vimtutor
page, which describes the Unix shell script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vim (1)
